**The plan is not ready to approve:** its measurement can miss lost questions and false merges, and several proposed rules go beyond the signed standard. For example, the stored week has a total-revenue question and a revenue-growth question that bypass the proposed same-type comparison; the plan’s own gold construction can miss that pair.

Findings are ranked by severity.

1. **The proposed gold can miss both false merges and missing required questions.** [Plan lines 100–101](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/research/2026-10-30-question-identity/plan.md:100) builds G1 from listed pairs plus unlisted pairs with the same object **and type**, and G2 from questions that already opened. In the v38 ledger, `v4` asks FY2027 total revenue and `v10` asks FY2027 revenue growth; match record 14 calls them different quantities. [D212](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/DECISIONS.md:2707) confirms that revenue/growth bypasses the same-measure gate. The pair can therefore be absent from G1 even if a future path merges it incorrectly. A required question never proposed or opened cannot enter G2 at all. The existing admission gold provides some missing-question coverage, but only for its specific cases ([D188](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/DECISIONS.md:2483)). A gold derived from source material, including required questions absent from the ledger and relevant cross-type pairs, is needed to detect these losses.

2. **The acceptance conditions allow material regressions to pass.** [Plan lines 124–126](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/research/2026-10-30-question-identity/plan.md:124) permit false merges up to the control’s count, even if the new arm loses a different required question. They count evidence as preserved if it is attached *anywhere*, even if it is attached to the wrong question. [D212](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/DECISIONS.md:2705) already records three material pieces under the wrong product question and says reducing page count did not restore dropped material. The evidence-dedup arm also has no stated acceptance threshold for G3 or a check that a different or richer claim remains visible to the judge; that was the loss behind [D204](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/DECISIONS.md:2611).

3. **H7’s proposed identity key can hide distinct evidence.** [Plan line 92](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/research/2026-10-30-question-identity/plan.md:92) treats equal speaker, date and numbers as one statement. One speaker can make two different claims about the same number on the same day, or add a qualification. Accurate fields do not establish equal meaning. The proposed single display also conflicts with the decision to show both source records to the judge, labelled as an opinion ([D201](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/DECISIONS.md:2587), [D204](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/DECISIONS.md:2612)). The plan names those decisions, but does not state this conflict.

4. **The claimed cause of the ACP split is unproven.** [Plan lines 12–16 and 68](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/research/2026-10-30-question-identity/plan.md:12) attribute the split to the “guarantee beside a financing” sentence. The sentence **is** in both [the collision prompt](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/src/hivemind/prompts/collision-v1.txt:1) and [the signed standard](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:318); the plan is correct on that factual point. But v38 match records 6 and 10 record only the verdicts, not the instruction that caused them. The plan itself acknowledges that the model account has not been obtained ([lines 75–76](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/research/2026-10-30-question-identity/plan.md:75)). The two standard lines create a real boundary to resolve, but the records do not establish that this sentence caused the split or that every guarantee and financing within a plan must be separate.

5. **H1, H3 and the general rule add boundaries that the standard does not settle.** [Plan lines 80–82 and 86–88](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/research/2026-10-30-question-identity/plan.md:80) add “when uncertain, merge,” “one plan, one question,” and “one product generation, one question.” The signed standard does say one outcome can settle two questions ([line 316](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:316)), so that part is correctly attributed. It also requires separation where answers can move apart ([line 274](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:274)), and [D236](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/DECISIONS.md:2871) permits a launch **or** shipment question; it does not decide that all milestones are one question. D243’s caution about noisy extraction is not a decision to merge uncertain questions ([standard lines 153–156](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:153)). The v38 ledger’s `v11` launch and `v17` shipment are a concrete case requiring that distinction.

6. **H4 treats different periods as a settled duplicate.** [Plan line 89](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/research/2026-10-30-question-identity/plan.md:89) says FY2027 CPU revenue and calendar-2026 server CPU revenue are the same question under the standard. They differ in both scope and period. The standard’s duplicate test concerns another presentation of the **same result** ([line 289](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:289)); it separately treats the next period as succession ([line 317](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:317)). The earlier [Claude-labelled review](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-admission-v12-2026-10-26/docs/research/2026-10-28-quality-review/gold-admission.md:30) labels this pair duplicate, but is not an Alex-approved decision.

7. **H2 and H5 do not fully cover the existing identity contract.** H2’s proposed merge keeps the earlier question’s fixed outcomes and due date; the plan does not show how a later deadline remains answerable after the earlier deadline passes. The existing question and outcomes are immutable ([PRD 06 lines 8 and 14](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/prd/06-views.md:8)); succession is continued tracking after an event question closes ([line 176](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/prd/06-views.md:176)). H5 says code would retain only object, type and due year ([plan line 90](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/research/2026-10-30-question-identity/plan.md:90)); that omits scope, event type and other distinctions currently used by [identity.py](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/src/hivemind/views/identity.py:18). It could coalesce separate events, and the plan does not enumerate that risk.

8. **M3’s cited mechanism and proposed repair do not cover all the cited misses.** [Plan lines 70 and 148](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/research/2026-10-30-question-identity/plan.md:70) combine peers missed by retrieval with peers excluded by type, but propose sending only same-object, same-type questions to the judge. That cannot cover the revenue/growth case above. The earlier review says four twins were outside the top ten, while also saying collision judging ran on all 11 candidates ([report lines 40–46](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-admission-v12-2026-10-26/docs/research/2026-10-28-quality-review/report.md:40)); those statements do not establish that the judge saw each missing twin. The actual gate requires both membership in the list and equal measure ([jev_matching.py](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/src/hivemind/views/jev_matching.py:195)).

9. **Several counts are presented more strongly than their sources allow.** The 69 questions, 80 candidates, 1 merge, 2 successions, and v38’s 17 questions, 19 candidates and 0 merges match the [census output](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/research/2026-10-30-question-identity/census/admission-census.txt:1). The 24/12/10/4 labels match the earlier [50-question review](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-admission-v12-2026-10-26/docs/research/2026-10-28-quality-review/gold-admission.md:58), but they are Claude’s unapproved judgments; 12 + 10 is 22 of 50, with four additional borderline cases. Thus [plan lines 8–10](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/research/2026-10-30-question-identity/plan.md:8) cannot establish that half should not exist or that the two causes are roughly equal. The 12 and 3 M1 counts are *verdict categories*, not verified duplicate errors. Further, the census classifies by parsing `reason` text ([script lines 19–34](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/research/2026-10-30-question-identity/census/admission_census.py:19)), contrary to the required field-based census ([AGENTS.md line 52](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/AGENTS.md:52)); the counts should be checked against the underlying records before being used as a mechanism census.

10. **“Different statements” is a model-label count, not a verified fact count.** The 1,888/1,168, 1,863/1,123, 52/27 and 46/29 figures match the stored census. The script collapses connected `same_claims` labels transitively ([week_counts.py lines 12–18](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/research/2026-10-30-question-identity/census/week_counts.py:12)); [D204](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/DECISIONS.md:2611) records eight incorrect or richer merges in 40 sampled labels. They are therefore counts *after collapsing matcher-labelled pairs*, not established counts of distinct claims. I independently verified that `v1` and `v3` share 20 evidence IDs in the v38 ledger ([plan line 62](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/research/2026-10-30-question-identity/plan.md:62)).

11. **The gold and experiment sequence needs clearer controls.** [Plan lines 104–109](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/research/2026-10-30-question-identity/plan.md:104) says both to label and resolve disagreements on the gold and that the holdout is not read before changes. It must distinguish reading source material to create a frozen holdout from exposing its labels or outcomes to the people tuning the arms. The plan also proposes directly using old admission gold ([line 112](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/research/2026-10-30-question-identity/plan.md:112)), while its [standard comparison](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/research/2026-10-29-analyst-standard/gold-check.md:3) says admission `must_not_open` labels need re-derivation for ledger-blind extraction. Finally, the plan schedules a rewrite addressing M1 **and M4** together ([line 145](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/research/2026-10-30-question-identity/plan.md:145)), so a regression cannot be attributed to one change as required by [AGENTS.md](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/AGENTS.md:292).

Other checks: D211’s ledger-blind extraction and D207’s narrowest-home placement are accurately represented for v38 ([decisions](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/DECISIONS.md:2680), [placement](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/DECISIONS.md:2630)). The diagram’s “top ten by wording” is an oversimplification: exact-key paths can supply the list instead ([matching.py](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/src/hivemind/views/matching.py:133)). H6’s worthwhile-to-track test is supported by the standard ([lines 280–287](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:280)); its claim that the model failed to apply it remains a diagnosis to prove, not an established cause.

I verified the principal counts and claims cited above, but did **not** independently verify every cost estimate, every census row’s classification, or the claim that all three M2 cases have the stated period-start mechanism. Those remain unverified rather than established errors. No files were edited.**Serious findings remain; the plan is not ready for approval.** For example, the revised gold can still miss a lost required question, and its evidence check can pass when evidence is attached to the wrong question.

1. **The required-question guard covers only selected old cases.** [Plan lines 105–107](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/research/2026-10-30-question-identity/plan.md:105) build G2 from questions that opened and G2′ from the existing admission and ACP golds. A required question absent from both the ledger and those selected cases remains invisible. Fixed extraction replay also cannot reveal a candidate the stored extraction never produced. [D212](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/DECISIONS.md:2707) records 94 material losses with no corresponding question during the week. The added G2′ improves round 1’s coverage but does not close it.

2. **The evidence-placement check can certify the wrong destination.** [Plan line 132](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/research/2026-10-30-question-identity/plan.md:132) checks that a merged candidate’s evidence reaches *the question it was merged into*. If the merge target itself is wrong, that check can pass. It also does not say how evidence dropped before or during writing is counted. The expected destination must come from the independently judged case; [D212](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/DECISIONS.md:2705) found three material records under the wrong product question.

3. **G1’s stated material omits evidence the collision judge actually reads.** [Plan line 105](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/research/2026-10-30-question-identity/plan.md:105) lists the candidate’s evidence but not the existing question’s evidence. [jev_matching.py lines 64–68](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/src/hivemind/views/jev_matching.py:64) supplies up to two existing evidence quotes per question. Those quotes appear in the stored ACP collision requests, including calls 66 and 236 in the [v38 archive](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/english-v38-nvda-1w-2026-10-28/archive.sqlite). A gold reader could therefore label a different case from the one the model saw.

4. **A hard case crosses objects, but the new gold is grouped by object.** [Plan lines 105–106](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/research/2026-10-30-question-identity/plan.md:105) add same-object pairs and judge each object’s questions separately. In the [sealed ledger](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/sealed-2026-10-28-v34-nvda-3m-through-0828/views.sqlite), `v40` asks about power allocation for the southern Ohio site under `chip-export-controls`; `v44` asks about approval of the Pike County campus arrangement under `NVDA`. The [earlier review line 42](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-admission-v12-2026-10-26/docs/research/2026-10-28-quality-review/report.md:42) groups them as the same Ohio matter. Whether their outcomes are identical needs source-based judgment; the current gold construction does not require that judgment.

5. **The ACP example still claims a contradiction and cause that the records do not prove.** [Plan lines 13–20](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/research/2026-10-30-question-identity/plan.md:13) and [line 77](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/research/2026-10-30-question-identity/plan.md:77) treat the three verdicts as mutually inconsistent and the standard’s two sentences as conflicting. The [signed standard lines 316–319](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:316) do contain both sentences, as the plan says, but whether they conflict depends on whether the quantities are parts of one program or independently answerable quantities. In the [v38 archive](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/english-v38-nvda-1w-2026-10-28/archive.sqlite), call 66 says `v3` is narrower than `v1`; call 236 compares a *different candidate* with both. That warrants investigation, not a logical contradiction by itself. The stored reasons also do not identify which prompt sentence caused the split; the planned model continuation is still needed.

6. **H4’s lean does not name the period conflict it creates.** [Plan line 94](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/research/2026-10-30-question-identity/plan.md:94) proposes folding a calendar-year question into a fiscal-year question because company quantities use fiscal years. But the example differs in both period and scope, and the [standard lines 274 and 316–317](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:274) distinguish one period, the same result, and a later period. The fiscal-year writing rule does not itself establish that these are the same result. H3 names its conflicting separation rule; H4 should likewise present this as an unresolved change to the identity boundary.

7. **The holdout does not have the promised independent disagreement check.** [Plan lines 112–114](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/research/2026-10-30-question-identity/plan.md:112) give the holdout to Codex alone but say disagreements go to Alex. With only one labeler, there is no second blind label to reveal disagreements. [AGENTS.md lines 246–251](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/AGENTS.md:246) require a blind second reader and decisions on disagreements. Separating the labels from the person tuning the prompt is a real improvement, but it does not replace that check.

8. **Some reported mechanisms and counts are still stronger than their evidence.** [Plan lines 8–10 and 81](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/research/2026-10-30-question-identity/plan.md:8) state that 22 questions should not exist and call M5 a traced mechanism. Those are the earlier author’s unapproved judgments, and M5 itself says the raw answers have not been checked. Line 81 also says four borderline cases, while the corrected count at line 9 is five. The [earlier gold’s individual rows](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-admission-v12-2026-10-26/docs/research/2026-10-28-quality-review/gold-admission.md:7) support 23 keep, 12 duplicate, 10 do not open, and five borderline—not the file’s own 24/12/10/4 summary.

