   The related statement that all D188 “must not open” cases should be set aside is too broad: [plan line 121](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/research/2026-10-30-question-identity/plan.md:121) cites the gold check, but it says many such cases remain valid and identifies the subset that should become “propose, then merge” cases ([gold check lines 62–65](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/research/2026-10-29-analyst-standard/gold-check.md:62)).

