**Yes, serious findings remain.****仍有严重问题：逐候选核对已经能发现不少误合并和漏题，但“应拒绝”的候选仍缺少明确的验收处理。** 例如，金标要求拒绝一个覆盖名单外的候选，而新版把它开成问题时，计划没有规定这类不一致是否使验收失败。

1. **严重：拒绝结果加入了金标，却没有加入停止条件。** [计划第 113 行](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/research/2026-10-30-question-identity/plan.md:113)增加了“应被规则拒”，但[第 151–159 行](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/research/2026-10-30-question-identity/plan.md:151)没有列出“应拒绝却新开或合并”及其停止条件。v38 的 [match record 29](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/english-v38-nvda-1w-2026-10-28/views.sqlite) 中，候选 `n1` 因对象不在覆盖名单被拒；[PRD 06 第 178 行](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/prd/06-views.md:178)允许这种拒绝。需要让**所有实际结局与金标不一致的情况都有明确处理**，才能说闭集的验收规则完整。

2. **严重：留出集会在连续改动中被反复用于决定下一步。** [计划第 166–167 行](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/research/2026-10-30-question-identity/plan.md:166)将留出集打分放在各次改动的流程里；[第 165、182 行](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/research/2026-10-30-question-identity/plan.md:165)又要求追查每个不一致、回归后再继续。这样后续改动可能已经利用了同一留出集的结果；“每个配置只打一次”不能防止这个问题。[AGENTS 第 256–258 行](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/AGENTS.md:256)要求在调试集调，测试集用于评分。应在调试集完成迭代后，再对最终配置使用留出集。

3. **重要难例：同一篇文章同时提出两个年度，现有续期路径接不上。** v38 的 [match record 14](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/english-v38-nvda-1w-2026-10-28/views.sqlite) 中，`c1` 和 `c2` 分别问同一组云厂商的 2026、2027 年资本开支，两者都判为新开，成为 `v8`、`v9`。[标准第 317 行](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:317)把同一量的下一期间列为续期；但[代码第 289–293 行](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/src/hivemind/views/matching.py:289)不允许候选续期到同一答案中的另一个候选。H2 讨论的是事件截止日，H1–H7 没有覆盖这个同篇年度接续的情形。G1 应明确标出这对的预期关系，并核对实际是否记录了该关系。

4. **事实错误：M4 把续期归因于碰撞裁决，证据不足。** [计划第 82 行](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/research/2026-10-30-question-identity/plan.md:82)说裁决判“下一期”，代码因此续期。但 v38 的 [match record 24](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/english-v38-nvda-1w-2026-10-28/views.sqlite)显示 Jev 自己也判了 `same_quantity_other_period`；[代码第 284–297 行](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/src/hivemind/views/jev_matching.py:284)在碰撞裁决前就可据此选续期，后面的裁决只保留了该结果。这个案例证明发生了续期，不能单独证明碰撞裁决造成了续期。

第 4 轮的结构规则**已补上**所指出的续期题、续期证据和到期后测试缺口；它也能在候选进入 G1 时发现错误合并和必需题丢失。上面的拒绝结局说明它还不能声称覆盖所有结局。两臂共同存在的绝对归档损失按要求留给 D212 审计。

核对过的主要事实包括：两本账的候选、合并和续期总数与[普查输出](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/research/2026-10-30-question-identity/census/admission-census.txt:1)一致；“担保和融资”确在[签字标准第 318 行](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:318)和碰撞提示词中，计划也已正确说明其是否导致 ACP 拆题尚未证明。H1–H7 的主要边界现已标为选择，H7 的倾向与 [D204](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/DECISIONS.md:2612)一致。裁决类别数仍依赖解析理由文字；我没有逐条验证全部归档裁决、费用估算和计划中的每一项事实。没有编辑文件。

**有严重问题仍需修正。****One serious finding remains:** the plan can accept a new duplicate if other duplicates are removed in the same arm.

1. **Serious — duplicate regressions can cancel out in the total.** [Plan lines 152–160](docs/research/2026-10-30-question-identity/plan.md#L152) compare each candidate with its expected outcome, but make missed merges an exception: the arm passes if their **number** is lower than the control. For example, two old duplicates could be fixed while a candidate that previously merged correctly opens a new duplicate; the total improves and the regression passes. This leaves part of the round-4 class open: the per-candidate record exposes the error, but the acceptance rule does not stop on it. The v38 census provides real merge cases to protect: [census lines 29–37](docs/research/2026-10-30-question-identity/census/admission-census.txt#L29) record 12 merges and three collision decisions classified as distinct within one matter.

2. **Factual, with measurement implications — the pipeline diagram puts placement after question matching.** [Plan lines 27–44](docs/research/2026-10-30-question-identity/plan.md#L27) show matching first and placement afterwards. In the current path, [round.py lines 103–130](src/hivemind/views/round.py#L103) obtains the extraction handover before matching, and [extraction.py lines 608–630](src/hivemind/extraction.py#L608) shows that placement is part of that handover. Placement can also remove a candidate when none of its evidence remains. The later measurement section correctly says placement may need a fresh answer when the open questions change, but the diagram and [line 145](docs/research/2026-10-30-question-identity/plan.md#L145) overstate that score changes come only from matching: placement sampling can change the candidate set too.

3. **Factual — the candidate-list description is too narrow.** [Plan line 34](docs/research/2026-10-30-question-identity/plan.md#L34) says the first route finds questions with the *same identity key*. [matching.py lines 122–145](src/hivemind/views/matching.py#L122) also includes compatible keys with overlapping periods; [store.py lines 161–172](src/hivemind/views/store.py#L161) specifies the overlap and wildcard rules. This matters to H5 because changing a period start can affect which questions are compared even when their full keys are unequal.

The round-4 fixes otherwise cover the listed successor, worthiness, evidence and holdout gaps: the gold now records those outcomes, and the future successor has a separate test. The two ACP sentences **are** in the signed standard ([lines 316–319](docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html#L316)); the plan correctly leaves their conflict and the prompt sentence’s causal role unresolved. H1–H7 name the relevant standard boundaries as choices, including the conflict H3 would introduce. I did not find another hard case in the two ledgers that requires a new H1–H7 mechanism.

The reported census totals match the saved census output, but I did not independently verify every archived verdict, quotation or estimate; the category script still parses reason text ([admission_census.py lines 18–37](docs/research/2026-10-30-question-identity/census/admission_census.py#L18)), as the plan itself acknowledges.

**Serious finding remains: yes — the missed-merge acceptance rule can hide a duplicate regression.****One serious finding remains:** the plan does not say how it will identify the same question across replay arms after question numbers change. For example, if the new arm merges away `v3`, a later, unrelated question can receive the number `v3`; comparing that number alone can make a wrong destination look right.

1. **Serious — the per-candidate check needs stable question identities across arms.** [Plan lines 114–117](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/research/2026-10-30-question-identity/plan.md:114) record the expected destination as an existing question `X`, and [lines 153–164](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/research/2026-10-30-question-identity/plan.md:153) compare that destination with each arm. But question IDs are assigned sequentially as questions are created ([writing.py, lines 22–25 and 37–38](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/src/hivemind/views/writing.py:22)). Removing one duplicate therefore shifts later IDs. The old replay script attempts translation by source item and question, but falls back to the old ID when it finds no match ([pinned_matching_study.py, lines 27–32 and 67–71](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/research/2026-10-26-thesis-admission-v12/pinned_matching_study.py:27)). The plan requires that script to reproduce the control, but does not specify how to resolve an old question that the new arm has merged away. A control can reproduce perfectly while the changed arm compares or files evidence against the wrong `v3`. The check needs a traceable mapping from each gold question to its actual question in each arm, including merged-away questions, and must stop if that mapping cannot be established.

2. **Factual — the revenue/growth example misstates Jev’s verdict.** [Plan line 82](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/research/2026-10-30-question-identity/plan.md:82) says Jev called v38’s total revenue and revenue growth questions unrelated. The [stored v38 ledger](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/english-v38-nvda-1w-2026-10-28/views.sqlite), inspected through [why_new.py](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/research/2026-10-30-question-identity/census/why_new.py:13), records candidate `c3` against `v4` as `same_matter_different_quantity`, probability `0.69`. The different measure still prevents the collision comparison ([jev_matching.py, lines 195–201](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/src/hivemind/views/jev_matching.py:195)); the recorded Jev reason should be corrected.

The round-4 structural rule now explicitly covers required successors, distinct but unworthy questions, and successor evidence; the future-deadline transition has a separate test ([plan lines 114–124 and 159–168](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/research/2026-10-30-question-identity/plan.md:114)). The round-8 duplicate regression is also a per-candidate stop condition. Those checks can detect false merges and lost required questions **once the cross-arm identity problem above is resolved**.

I verified the main census counts by rerunning its read-only script on all five ledgers, and verified the 20 shared evidence records between v38 `v1` and `v3`. The census verdict categories remain provisional because the script parses reason text ([admission_census.py, lines 18–37](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/research/2026-10-30-question-identity/census/admission_census.py:18)). I also checked the ACP archive: call 66 and call 236 compare different candidates, as the revised plan says. The guarantee-and-financing sentence is in both the [signed standard](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:316) and the [collision prompt](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/src/hivemind/prompts/collision-v1.txt:1); the stored reasons do not establish that it caused the split.

I found no additional uncovered hard case in the two ledgers that requires a new H1–H7 mechanism. The leans name the relevant standard boundaries, and H7 preserves D204. I could not independently verify every archived quotation, cost estimate, or the full question context behind Alex’s two recorded “A” replies; those remain unverified rather than assumed correct.

**Serious finding remains: yes — cross-arm question identity is not yet defined for the acceptance comparison.****A serious finding remains:** the plan says every new regression stops an arm, but also says a newly opened trivial question will only be counted. For example, if the control keeps a minor candidate as evidence and the changed matcher opens it as a separate question, the plan gives two different acceptance rules.

1. **Serious — a new trivial question can pass.** [Plan lines 155–156]( /Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/research/2026-10-30-question-identity/plan.md:155) make every candidate that was correct in the control and wrong in the new arm a stopping condition. But [line 165]( /Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/research/2026-10-30-question-identity/plan.md:165) exempts a distinct but unworthy question from stopping a matching arm. The [signed standard]( /Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:281) requires both distinctness and worth. The plan needs to distinguish an **existing** unworthy opening, which can be reported as a remaining defect, from a **new** one caused by the changed arm, which its own regression rule says must stop it.

2. **Factual — the placement diagram overstates the one-home rule.** [Plan lines 33–34]( /Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/research/2026-10-30-question-identity/plan.md:33) say placement files each statement under the narrowest existing question **or** this article’s candidate. In [placement.py]( /Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/src/hivemind/placement.py:63), candidate links from extraction are retained and the placer’s existing-question links are added. A statement can therefore have both. This matters when recording every expected evidence destination.

3. **Factual — 94 statements without a question are not 94 questions never proposed.** [Plan line 124]( /Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/research/2026-10-30-question-identity/plan.md:124) uses D212’s count to describe an extraction coverage gap. [D212]( /Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/DECISIONS.md:2705) says 94 **material records** had no corresponding question during the week; it does not establish that no candidate was proposed. The [underlying trace]( /Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/research/2026-10-28-retention-audit/root-trace-2026-10-28.md:7) also cautions that these are records, not 94 different facts. Losses common to both arms remain outside this review’s measurement scope.

The per-candidate rule otherwise addresses the round-4 examples: it represents required successors, distinguishes worth from identity, checks successor evidence, and adds an expiry test. The round-9 fix also provides a way to translate question IDs across arms. The stored v38 same-article 2026 and 2027 spending questions remain a known hard case: [the plan records their missing succession relationship but does not propose changing it]( /Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/research/2026-10-30-question-identity/plan.md:119); the [PRD]( /Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/prd/06-views.md:133) says successive periods form a chain.

I verified the main census totals by rerunning the read-only script, and verified the 20 shared evidence records in v38. The guarantee-and-financing example is in both the [signed standard]( /Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:314) and the [collision prompt]( /Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/src/hivemind/prompts/collision-v1.txt:1); the plan correctly leaves its causal role in the ACP split unproven. The verdict-category census still parses reason text, as the plan says. I could not independently verify every archived verdict, cost estimate, or the full question context behind the “A” replies in section 11b.

**Serious finding remains: yes.****仍有两项严重问题：逐候选核对还可能漏掉候选，而且同篇文章里的续期关系被排除在验收之外。** 例如，改变已有问题后，归档可能让一个原先没进入匹配的候选进入匹配；如果金标只收原账本里的候选，这个新结果就没人核对。

1. **严重：金标的候选范围可能漏掉新臂出现的候选。** [计划第 122、125 行](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/research/2026-10-30-question-identity/plan.md:122)把五个账本里已有的候选当作完整范围；但[第 151 行](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/research/2026-10-30-question-identity/plan.md:151)也承认，问题变化后归档要重新发送。代码先按归档结果丢弃没有落点的证据，再移除失去全部证据的候选，之后才保存交接记录、进入匹配（[extraction.py 第 608 行](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/src/hivemind/extraction.py:608)、[第 746 行](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/src/hivemind/extraction.py:746)、[round.py 第 119 行](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/src/hivemind/views/round.py:119)）。因此，固定抽取答案里一个原先被归档移除的候选，可能因新臂的已有问题不同而留下并开题，却不在原账本金标里。应从**归档前的固定抽取候选**建立核对范围，并把归档移除也记为实际结局；这检查的是两臂之间的变化，不扩大到共同丢失证据的 D212 审计。

2. **严重：同篇候选的续期关系被记下，却不参与验收。** [计划第 119–120 行](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/research/2026-10-30-question-identity/plan.md:119)明确说同篇两年的候选都按新开处理，只记录缺失的续期关系；这与[第 108 行](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/research/2026-10-30-question-identity/plan.md:108)“每个候选的完整结局都核对”的说法不一致。v38 的 `v8` 和 `v9` 来自同一文章，分别问 2026 和 2027 年云厂商资本开支；只读查询显示两题都存在，但续期表没有 `v9 → v8`。现行 [PRD 06 第 133–136 行](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/prd/06-views.md:133)要求同一关注点的连续期间组成链。这不是少开了一题，但关系仍错；计划需要把它作为明确的剩余错误纳入结局核对，不能称为完整闭集。

已核实的主要部分：两本账本的候选、合并和续期总数与[普查输出](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/research/2026-10-30-question-identity/census/admission-census.txt:1)一致；v38 的 `v1` 和 `v3` 确有 20 条共同证据。裁决类别仍由[脚本解析理由文字](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/research/2026-10-30-question-identity/census/admission_census.py:25)，计划已标明需用结构化答案重数。担保与融资的例子确实同时出现在[签字标准](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:318)和[裁决提示词](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/src/hivemind/prompts/collision-v1.txt:1)；计划现在正确地把它是否造成拆题、以及它与 D210 的边界是否冲突，留作待确认问题。

H1–H7 的倾向已把主要标准边界标成选择；H7 保留两条证据，符合 [D204](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/DECISIONS.md:2611)。第 4 轮指出的必开续期、值得开与否、续期证据和未来到期测试，计划都有了对应检查；上面两项是完整覆盖仍有的缺口。第 11b 节只记录了简短的“A”，我无法独立核实每个回答所对应的完整提问；也没有逐一核实所有存档裁决和费用估计。

