376:- D44: initial model-owned identity and step-4 matching. D45: distinguish recorded decisions from proposals; similar questions remain separate. D155 later bounds code-owned identity in the POC.
377:- D46/D49: one state, concrete ladders, ordinary ingestion of decisive evidence, years based on publication day, top-N whole-library search.
382:- D54: freeze the current state when due; no separate result or extra wait; pull mode owns time.
393:- D149 requirement: organise theses by the continuing business process they discuss, called a research group. Vera Rubin readiness and customer deployment can share a group while shipment dates, SK factory launch and OpenAI deployment retain separate questions, ladders and due dates. A group may start with one thesis; a thesis may belong to several groups. A group has no state or ladder, creates no automatic dependency and is not an overarching investment thesis for an agent.
399:- Acceptance measures source-supported membership and evidence retention, not identical names, IDs or group counts on every run. Report omissions, check refusals, missed associations and wrong associations separately. Preserve Rubin shipment/customer-deployment relationships and check wrong links to unrelated products or customer-specific groups. Multi-company and large-library behaviour is not yet validated.

